(* Premise L5: "the input ring's drop: a writer that asks `room` and posts
   within it never overwrites" (planning/mvp-m8-plan.md, D-3 and D-9), the
   premise of P3 (e), input_ring_drops_under_room
   (planning/mvp-m8-specifications.md, sections 1 and 3, specification
   SHA-256 ade32fa639d255ec2ba08040bbe8dbba2d7d8bf3fc4401947f4c542ecc9dc53d).
   As L3 and L4, on the input ring: the room read, the branch, the post or
   the drop count, as compiled in build/mvp/gcc/be-mvp.elf and
   build/mvp/clang/be-mvp.elf (the lines in
   mvp/verify/litmus/sequences/SYMBOL-TOOLCHAIN.s; GCC's address, then
   Clang's): the ring full (4096 bytes posted, none released), the
   domain hart releasing an INPUT record of 24 bytes (8 typed bytes) while
   hart 0 flushes 8 more, which fit only in the bytes it frees.
   P0, the domain hart in be_mvp_dispatch's console_read:
     lbu x5,0(x10)   the INPUT's first byte, 97, be_mvp_ring_take, called
                     by be_mvp_input_serve at 10206a4a8 and 10206ad30,
                     called at 10206638c and 10206641a
                                                        102068836 102068d96
     fence r,w       be_mvp_arch_fence_r_w, through be_mvp_exec_fence_r_w,
                     called at                          1020663a0 10206642a
     sd x12,0(x11)   the tail, 24, be_mvp_ring_release  102068876 102068e10
   P1, hart 0 in be_mvp_input_flush, called by poll_input at 10206499a and
   10206576e:
     ld x5,0(x10)    be_mvp_ring_room: the tail         1020685c0 102068b50
     sub x6,x13,x5   used = cursor - tail               1020685d4 102068b64
     sub x7,x12,x6   free = capacity - used (GCC: tail - cursor + capacity,
                     1020685ea and 1020685ec)                     102068b74
     li x8,0         no room (GCC: the aligned tail's low bits, 0, by
                     andi a0,a5,7)                      1020685c2 102068b7e
     bge x9,x7,LC00  16 or fewer free: no room          1020685f0 102068b7a
     addi x8,x7,-16  the payload room                   1020685f4 102068b84
     andi x8,x8,-8   rounded down to 8                  102068602 102068b92
     LC00:
     beq x8,x0,LC01  be_mvp_input_flush: no room, the batch dropped
                                                        10206a328 10206ab78
     ld x14,0(x10)   be_mvp_ring_post: the tail again   1020684ce 102068a3a
     sub x15,x13,x14 used                               1020684e6 102068a56
     sub x16,x12,x15 free                               1020684fe 102068a6a
     blt x16,x17,LC02 the room check, refused below 24  102068504 102068a6e
     sb x18,0(x11)   the batch's first byte, 98         1020685a4 102068b22
     j LC02
     LC01:
     sd x19,0(x20)   the drop count, hart 0's own word  10206a082 10206abea
     LC02:
   be_mvp_ring_room's cap of 256 (a branch on the same value, 1020685fe and
   102068b8a) and be_mvp_input_flush's choice of the room or the pending
   bytes (10206a322 and 10206ab72) leave these values as they are, so the
   test leaves them out; L4 holds be_mvp_ring_post's other branches on the
   tail. The compiled branches are bgeu, beqz, and bltu: herd7 7.58
   implements no bltu, bgeu, or sltu for RISC-V ("RISCV operation bltu is
   not implemented (yet)") and no beqz, so the test branches with bge,
   beq against x0, and blt on the same registers, whose values stay below
   2^63, where the comparisons agree; herd7's ctrl follows the branch's
   registers, not its comparison. Clang's no-room answer is li a1,0;
   GCC's is the aligned tail's low bits, whose zero the test loads with
   li. A reduced test keeps fewer accesses and orderings than the code, so
   it allows at least the code's outcomes: Never here is Never there.
   Forbidden: the domain hart's load of the INPUT's first byte reads the
   next batch's while hart 0's room read of the tail reads the release.
